 displayed here.</p></div><div class="company-tab-content" id="balance-sheet"><p class="tech-description">Balance Sheet details will be displayed here.</p></div><div class="company-tab-content" id="dividend-history"><p class="tech-description">Dividend History details will be displayed here.</p></div><div class="company-tab-content" id="comparative-return"><p class="tech-description">Comparative Return details will be displayed here.</p></div></div>		<div class="container"><div class="faq-header"><h2 class="faq-title">FAQ<span>'s</span></h2><p class="faq-subtitle">Answers to all your trading related queries.</p></div><div class="faq-accordion"><div class="faq-item active"><div class="faq-question"><span class="faq-question-text">Can I start trading once my account is activated?</span>&nbsp;<svg class="faq-chevron" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></div><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-content">Any Indian resident/non-resident individual (not US-based) or Indian corporate can register with HDFC securities Ltd for trading. Currently, overseas corporate bodies (OCBs) cannot open an account with HDFC securities. To become a registered user of HDFC securities, you will have to first open a savings/current account and demat account with HDFC Bank.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question"><span class="faq-question-text">How many bank and depository accounts can I link to a trading account?</span>&nbsp;<svg class="faq-chevron" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></div><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-content">You can link multiple bank accounts and depository accounts to your trading account. However, at any given time, only one bank account and one depository account can be active for trading purposes. You can switch between linked accounts through your online trading portal or by contacting our customer support.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question"><span class="faq-question-text">Can I start trading once my account is activated?</span>&nbsp;<svg class="faq-chevron" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></div><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-content">Yes, once your account is activated, you can start trading immediately. You will receive your login credentials via email and SMS. Simply log in to the trading platform, deposit funds into your linked bank account, and you're ready to place your first trade.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question"><span class="faq-question-text">How do I track my application status?</span>&nbsp;<svg class="faq-chevron" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></div><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-content">You can track your application status by logging into the HDFC securities portal and navigating to the "My Applications" section. You will also receive email and SMS notifications at each stage of the application process. If you face any issues, you can contact our support team with your application reference number.</div></div></div></div></div>
\.


